{
  "_": [
    "turtles_pro on the same table as turtles_le.vpxmap.json, made from it by tmnt_pro_map.py:",
    "every switch, coil and LED renumbered by name through the Pro's rig tables. The Pro has no",
    "van lock (the Party Wagon's LOWER LOCK 1/2 and its coil), so the table's van holds no ball.",
    "PAD-811: the LE card does not start a game in the emulator (rigbatch startcheck: 'no game",
    "started after three tries'; the Pro passes), so the Pro is what the table plays today.",
    "turtles_le on Bigus / Cheese3075's 'Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles (Stern-Data East mash-up)' v2.86d:",
    "Stern's 2020 TMNT playfield (art, inserts, the Party Wagon, LAIR and APRIL banks) whose rules were",
    "Data East's 1991 tmnt_104 ROM. The body is the LE's (the van, the van door/lock, one right spinner),",
    "not the Pro's (no van, an upper shooter lane). This map is what patch_turtles_le.py applies to its",
    "script, and what padcontroller.py serves. Numbers: switch 1000+id (switch_list.txt), lamp",
    "1000+node*100+index (led_io.txt), solenoid: the small number under `solenoids`.",
    "The rig's turtles_le tables carry NO positions (switch_xy absent, device_xy all 0), so every",
    "match is by the table's object names, their surfaces (which ramp a trigger rides), the Stern art",
    "under each light, and the table script's own comments. GUESS = wants a look at the machine."
  ],
  "title": "turtles_pro",
  "detect": [
    "tmnt_104",
    "Bigus / Cheese3075"
